# Project View environment variables.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. Each variable lists where it must be set:
#   Local    your .env / .env.*.local files
#   Vercel   Vercel project env (Production and/or Preview)
#   GitHub   GitHub Actions repo secret, read by the shared CI in
#            crashoutcompany/.github
#
# The app runs without these (search is disabled until all three are set).
# The CI build pulls them from Vercel, so they don't need GitHub secrets.

# Local, Vercel (Production + Preview). YouTube Data API v3 key.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=""
# Local, Vercel (Production + Preview). Upstash Redis (Vercel KV integration).
KV_REST_API_URL=""
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=""

# --- GitHub Actions only (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions) -----
# VERCEL_TOKEN=""        GitHub secret. CI `vercel build`.
# VERCEL_ORG_ID=""       GitHub secret. CI `vercel build` (optional if .vercel is linked).
# VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=""   GitHub secret. CI `vercel build` (optional if .vercel is linked).
